paths: {YREC_INPUT} set becomes its value                              ok
paths: {YREC_START} unset becomes ../../startmodels                    ok
paths: {YREC_OUTPUT} empty becomes output                              ok
paths: {YREC_INPUT} unset becomes ../../input                          ok
paths: no leading placeholder, the value unchanged                     ok
paths: an expansion to a later placeholder is expanded again           ok
directories: the path up to its last '/'                               ok
directories: blank for a bare file name                                ok
pulse format: GYRE, FGONG, GSM in any case                             ok
pulse format: leading and trailing blanks ignored                      ok
pulse format: any other name unknown                                   ok
fields: a number that fits is an I<width> field                        ok
fields: a wider one in full after a blank, no asterisks                ok
fields: the interior GYRE file's model number, 5 digits or all         ok
columns: a blank file name selects the defaults, in order              ok
columns: a file selects its names in order, past comments              ok
columns: an unknown name is an error                                   ok
columns: the run log lists the valid names                             ok
columns: a file that selects nothing is an error                       ok
columns: a missing file is an error                                    ok
columns: more than max_cols names is an error                          ok
groups: found in any case, after blanks                                ok
groups: a blank, a tab or '/' may end the name                         ok
groups: not a prefix of a longer name, nor a comment                   ok
groups: none in a comment, none in a missing file                      ok
.mod: read back without error                                          ok
.mod: every global value bit for bit                                   ok
.mod: every shell's structure bit for bit                              ok
.mod: every shell's composition bit for bit, in its slot               ok
.mod: the columns line, and a row in its order                         ok
.mod: replace keeps one model, append adds one                         ok
.mod: an unknown global is noted and skipped                           ok
.mod: another columns line is an error                                 ok
.mod: a file cut inside its shells is an error                         ok
.mod: a zone count above json is an error                              ok
format tag: the first four characters, from the start                  ok
format tag: an empty file is an error                                  ok
YREC7: read without error                                              ok
YREC7: the header and the flags                                        ok
YREC7: MODEL2's header values at their defaults                        ok
YREC7: the shells' structure                                           ok
YREC7: X and Z in units of 1e-6                                        ok
YREC7: He3-O18 per shell, copied through the convection zones          ok
YREC7: He4 = 1 - X - Z - He3                                           ok
YREC7: H2-Be9 two shells per line, the odd one alone                   ok
YREC7: omega from -log10(omega), zero at the sentinel                  ok
YREC7: the envelope records, the triangle reflected                    ok
YREC7: luminosities in Lsun kept                                       ok
YREC7: luminosities in erg/s converted to Lsun                         ok
YREC7: no negative record number, the triangle as it is                ok
YREC7: a rotating file without omega reads, omega zero                 ok
YREC7: a file cut inside its shells is an error                        ok
YREC7: a zone count of 0 is an error                                   ok
YREC7: a shell mass above the star's is an error                       ok
YREC7: an envelope convection zone outside the model is an error       ok
MODEL2: read without error                                             ok
MODEL2: the header                                                     ok
MODEL2: the codes, the flags and the disk constants                    ok
MODEL2: the luminosities and the envelope records                      ok
MODEL2: every shell's columns                                          ok
MODEL2: a file cut inside its shells is an error                       ok
MODEL2: a zone count above json is an error                            ok
tables: history names nonblank, short enough and unique                ok
tables: history kinds real_column or integer_column                    ok
tables: history default selection resolves, in order                   ok
tables: profile names nonblank, short enough and unique                ok
tables: profile kinds real_column or integer_column                    ok
tables: profile default selection resolves, in order                   ok
writes: a failed write of the .mod model is an error                   ok
writes: a failed history row is an error                               ok
writes: a failed write of the isochrone file is an error               ok
writes: a file whose directory cannot be made is an error              ok
writes: a GYRE file cut short by a full disk is an error               ok
writes: an FGONG file cut short by a full disk is an error             ok
writes: a profile cut short by a full disk is an error                 ok
writes: a history row cut short by a full disk is an error             ok
writes: a .mod model cut short by a full disk is an error              ok
writes: an isochrone file cut short by a full disk is an error         ok
writes: a run log cut short by a full disk is an error                 ok
writes: a run log rewound and written shorter is not cut short         ok
writes: a copy of the deck cut short by a full disk is an error        ok
writes: a history file another run truncated is not a full disk        ok
writes: a history file another run replaced is not a full disk         ok
writes: a closed file is measured, not the one now at its path         ok
writes: the size check keeps the unit's place in its file              ok
